#---
# purpose: "fz-bsx.3 — nested structural == of a heap binary vs a utf8 string agrees on all paths (run/build match interp)"
#---
#
# # bsx_nested_eq
#
# Regression guard for fz-bsx: `Utf8.from_bytes(<<104,105>>) == {:ok, "hi"}`
# compares a heap binary nested in a tuple against a utf8 string literal. The
# brand is type-system metadata; runtime equality is bytewise, so every path
# must agree (`true`). Before fz-bsx, native `run`/`build` folded this to `false`.
import Utf8

fn main() do
  good = <<104, 105>>
  r = Utf8.from_bytes(good)
  dbg(r == {:ok, "hi"})
  dbg({:ok, good} == {:ok, "hi"})
end
